From 45f8d3880bef68894da93097995e546a1204bbea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shardul Bankar <shardul.b@mpiricsoftware.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 02:43:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mptcp: extend kcov instrumentation to the option parser

The commit "mptcp: instrument MP_JOIN validity gates with kcov"
wrapped three subflow-level validity gates but explicitly
deferred mptcp_parse_option -- the per-suboption parse dispatch
-- noting "no clean way to reach the relevant msk from a bare
sk_buff without an invasive refactor."

This adds that coverage without the refactor.  mptcp_parse_option
is reached only through mptcp_get_options(), and the sole caller
of mptcp_get_options() in options.c is mptcp_incoming_options(),
which already derives the parent msk from the subflow socket at
function entry.  Wrapping the mptcp_get_options() call there --
not the parser itself -- gives the parser an active kcov_remote
region keyed on the msk's handle, with no signature change.

mptcp_incoming_options() runs in softirq on every incoming
segment of an established connection, so without this the
per-suboption parsing of ADD_ADDR / RM_ADDR / MP_PRIO / MP_FAIL /
MP_RST / DSS contributes no coverage to a kcov-driven fuzzer.
That is the surface the BRF protocol-flow harness's wire-level
option mutations target; coverage feedback there is what lets a
coverage-guided fuzzer evolve toward the deeper parse paths.

The other mptcp_get_options() call sites all live in subflow.c
(subflow establishment and data-ready paths) and are not wrapped
here: the load-bearing MP_JOIN validity gates already carry their
own kcov regions from the preceding patch, and not all of those
call sites have an msk in scope.

BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_START / _STOP reduce to a single branch when the
msk carries no handle, and compile to nothing when CONFIG_KCOV=n.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-7
Signed-off-by: Shardul Bankar <shardul.b@mpiricsoftware.com>
---
 net/mptcp/options.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/mptcp/options.c b/net/mptcp/options.c
index 4cc583fdc7a9c..58cba581f7907 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/options.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/options.c
@@ -1188,7 +1188,13 @@ bool mptcp_incoming_options(struct sock *sk, struct sk_buff *skb)
 		return true;
 	}
 
+	/* BRF kcov: cover the softirq-context option parser so the
+	 * wire-mutation harness gets feedback for ADD_ADDR / RM_ADDR /
+	 * MP_PRIO / MP_FAIL / DSS parsing.  Wrapped here (msk in scope)
+	 * rather than inside mptcp_get_options(), which sees only skb. */
+	BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_START(msk);
 	mptcp_get_options(skb, &mp_opt);
+	BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_STOP(msk);
 
 	/* The subflow can be in close state only if check_fully_established()
 	 * just sent a reset. If so, tell the caller to ignore the current packet.

base-commit: 7e6dbef35ec947d15465f814a198a6872ffc9911
